; Sound effect requested
;
; Written by the game code to start a sound effect, cleared by #R$871A (the routine called each frame through the
; interrupt) when it picks the request up. 1 is a special short sound built in the routine, 2-9 are the 8-byte
; descriptions at #R$87F2 (effect n at $87F2+8*(n-2)). Known requests: 3 bell or lever touched (#R$A748), 4 passage
; between rooms 10 and 19 (#R$A6D8), 5 item taken, wheel turned, chalice, key accepted in the controls menu (#R$A70B,
; #R$A6A1, #R$A3B9), 6 the player dies (#R$AA3D), 8 the church door (#R$A615), 9 checkpoint touched (#R$A688). On a
; 128K machine the AY player handles the request instead (#R$85D5).
@label=SoundRequest
g$854F DEFB $00
